<title>USA: Intel still seen as buy at Bear Stearns.</title>
<headline>Intel still seen as buy at Bear Stearns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear Stearns &amp; Co chip analyst Andy Neff still considers Intel a buy because of strong new products in the works and little threat from competitors, a source at the investment bank said Thursday.</p>
<p>Neff told traders at the firm this morning that he still expects Intel's Pentium II chip -- to be introduced later this year -- to sell well, the source said.</p>
<p>Neff also said a new fast chip from Advanced Micro Devices Inc poses little threat to Intel.</p>
</text>
